<title>BAHRAIN: TABLE-UNITED GULF BANK FIRST HALF NET RISES.</title>
<headline>TABLE-UNITED GULF BANK FIRST HALF NET RISES.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			     (million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p> Net income		   16.3   vs    5.2</p>
<p> Investment income	  19.7   vs    8.2</p>
<p> Interest income	     4.5   vs    7.0</p>
<p> Net operating income     17.9   vs   10.1</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity    238.7   vs  225.2</p>
<p> Total assets		380.7   vs  339.2</p>
<p>Full Name: United Gulf Bank E.C.</p>
<p>Note - The Bahrain-based offshore investment bank is 97 percent owned by Kuwait Investment Projects Company. The bank said it had recently completed acquisition of a stake of about 38 percent in Amman-based Jordan Kuwait Bank and 22.7 percent stake in Baltijas Tranzitu Banka (Baltic Transit Bank) in Riga, Latvia.</p>
</text>
